Sensor Suite: Input, Output, and Closed-Loop Control Architecture

Platform: AgentVerse Kinematic Quintet (Paddy Field Multi-Robot System)

1. Executive Summary

In flooded, mud-heavy rice paddies, conventional vision systems get blinded by
spray and foliage, while GPS signals suffer severe attenuation under dense wet
canopies. The Kinematic Quintet replaces heavy optical sensing with a ruggedized
sensor fusion suite combining high-frequency inertial sensing, millimeter-wave
radar, mechanical tactile whiskers, load strain gauges, and a dual-antenna
UWB/RF mast. This document details every sensor's physical input, processed
digital output, and the deterministic physical control action it triggers on the
robot.

